{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 21, :comments ["<b>But if a day</b> — this verse begins with alef and ends with alef, to teach that he must live twenty-four hours (from time to time)." "<b>יוקם</b> — three times in the Masorah: here, and the others: יוקם קין (Genesis 4:15), כל הרג קין שבעתים יקם (Genesis 4:24). This is what they said: one who sells his slave for thirty days — Rabbi Meir says the first is subject to judgment for 'a day or two days,' and not the second, since the acquisition of produce is not like the acquisition of the body. And this is 'לא יוקם כי כספו הוא' — and which is the 'כסף' of 'יוקם קין'? That one whose body is acquired by him, as it is written: קניתי איש את HaShem." "<b>כספו</b> — in gematria כדין לכהמה, for even regarding an animal, twenty-four hours (from time to time) is required for the matter of crushed limbs."], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-12T19:13:56.856840377Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}